## Implementation Blueprint

### Phase 1: Foundation Setup
**Priority: CRITICAL - Must complete before any other development**

#### 1.1 Project Initialization
```bash
# Create Vite + React project
npm create vite@latest design-studio --template react-ts
cd design-studio
npm install

# Install core dependencies
npm install @blueprintjs/core @blueprintjs/icons @blueprintjs/datetime2
npm install react-konva konva
npm install goober
npm install zustand immer
```

#### 1.2 Blueprint.js Dark Theme Setup
**Critical Configuration Steps:**
```javascript
// src/main.tsx - MUST include these imports
import 'normalize.css/normalize.css';
import '@blueprintjs/core/dist/css/blueprint.css';
import '@blueprintjs/icons/dist/css/blueprint-icons.css';

// Add dark theme class to body
document.body.classList.add('bp5-dark');
```

#### 1.3 Goober CSS-in-JS Configuration
```javascript
// src/main.tsx - Setup Goober with React
import { setup } from 'goober';
import React from 'react';

setup(React.createElement);
```

#### 1.4 Three-Panel Layout Structure
**Exact Layout Specifications:**
- **Left Panel**: 72px minimum width, expandable to 300px
- **Center Panel**: Flexible width (fills remaining space)
- **Right Panel**: Fixed 350px width, collapsible
- **Theme**: Dark mode (#2f343c background) with Blueprint.js components

**Blueprint.js Dark Theme Implementation:**
```javascript
// Apply dark theme globally
document.body.classList.add('bp4-dark');

// For specific components
<div className="bp4-dark">
  <NavigationPanel />
  <CanvasArea />
  <ToolsPanel />
</div>

// For dynamic components like popovers
<Popover2 popoverClassName="bp4-dark">
  {/* content */}
</Popover2>
```

### Phase 2: Canvas System Implementation
**Priority: HIGH - Core functionality**

#### 2.1 Konva.js Integration
**Key Implementation Points:**
- Use `react-konva` for React integration
- Implement HTML5 Canvas with WebGL acceleration
- Support infinite zoom (10% to 500% range)
- Enable multi-page/artboard functionality

**Reference Code Pattern:**
```javascript
import { Stage, Layer, Rect, Text, Circle } from 'react-konva';

// Follow patterns from https://konvajs.org/docs/react/Shapes.html
// Implement transform controls from https://konvajs.org/docs/sandbox/Canvas_Editor.html
```

#### 2.2 Element Transform System
**Required Controls:**
- 8-point bounding box for resize operations
- Rotation handle with snap angles (15°, 30°, 45°, 90°)
- Multi-selection with lasso tool
- Real-time transform feedback
- Smart alignment guides with snap zones

#### 2.3 Undo/Redo State Management
**Technical Requirements:**
- Immutable state trees supporting 100+ operations
- Zustand store for canvas state
- Command pattern implementation for actions

**Recommended Implementation Pattern:**
```javascript
// Command Pattern for Undo/Redo
class CanvasCommand {
  execute() { /* implement action */ }
  undo() { /* implement reverse action */ }
}

// Zustand store structure
const useCanvasStore = create((set, get) => ({
  elements: [],
  history: [],
  historyIndex: -1,
  
  executeCommand: (command) => {
    command.execute();
    const { history, historyIndex } = get();
    const newHistory = history.slice(0, historyIndex + 1);
    newHistory.push(command);
    set({ history: newHistory, historyIndex: newHistory.length - 1 });
  },
  
  undo: () => {
    const { history, historyIndex } = get();
    if (historyIndex >= 0) {
      history[historyIndex].undo();
      set({ historyIndex: historyIndex - 1 });
    }
  },
  
  redo: () => {
    const { history, historyIndex } = get();
    if (historyIndex < history.length - 1) {
      history[historyIndex + 1].execute();
      set({ historyIndex: historyIndex + 1 });
    }
  }
}));
```

